## Definitions

**"Software"** means the original work and any portion thereof.

**"Modified Version"** means any work that incorporates, alters, extends, adapts, derives from, or is based on the Software.

**"Forked Version"** means any independently distributed Modified Version that is not solely an internal/private modification.

**"Source Code"** means the preferred form of the work for making modifications.

**"Downstream Recipient"** means any person or entity receiving the Software or any Modified Version.

---

## Grant of Rights

Subject to compliance with this License, each recipient is granted a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, modify, and distribute the Software.

---

## Contribution Requirement Upon Distribution

Any person or entity that distributes a Modified Version or Forked Version shall:

1. Make available the complete corresponding Source Code of that Modified Version under this same License; and  
2. Ensure the Source Code is provided either:
   - Along with the distributed work, or  
   - Through a publicly accessible repository maintained for at least three (3) years after the last distribution of that version.

---

## Reciprocal Fork Return Requirement (Core Reciprocity Clause)

Any Forked Version must be made available under this License and must be:

1. Returned upstream to the original Software project (or its designated maintainer, if any), and  
2. Shared downstream, such that every Downstream Recipient of that Forked Version is also granted the same rights under this License, including access to Source Code.

This obligation applies recursively to all subsequent Forked Versions, such that every Fork inherits the same requirement to return improvements upstream and propagate the same rights downstream.

---

## Preservation of Improvements

Any modification, bug fix, enhancement, optimization, extension, or additional functionality incorporated into a distributed Modified Version or Forked Version shall be licensed under this License.

No distributor may impose additional restrictions that would prevent any recipient from exercising the rights granted herein.

---

## Transitive Reciprocity Obligation

All rights and obligations under this License are:

- Perpetual  
- Irrevocable (except under Termination below)  
- Transitive, applying equally to all downstream recipients  

No recipient may break the chain of obligations by re-licensing, privatizing, or restricting any Forked Version.

---

## Attribution

Copies and Modified Versions must preserve:

- Copyright notices  
- License notices  
- A record of material modifications  

